# netsurf: sibling-rule scan reads *, comments before @font-face, plain pseudo-classes in a left compound, nth-*(An+B), :has(> x); a parsed :has() reaches 198's check (patch 413)
# Generated 2026-11-08
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 412)
#
# The remaining "sibling combinator may restyle on insert/remove" declines
# after 412. A scratch debug build logged each prelude that still made a
# sheet "conservative" (state 2: every block insert/remove declines):
#
#  - a bare universal compound, ".x > *": parse_compound returned -1 for
#    a compound of only "*" (rte, google);
#  - Google Fonts' "/* latin-ext */ @font-face {": the prelude start skipped
#    white space but not comments, so the at-rule was taken for a selector
#    and its descriptors ("U+0100-024F;") parsed as one (rte, oldreddit);
#  - a plain pseudo-class in a sibling rule's LEFT compound,
#    ".gb_Ac:first-child+.gb_qc": any pseudo there declined;
#  - ":nth-last-child(2) ~" -- an nth-*() of An+B only;
#  - ":has(> article...)": :has()'s argument could not open with ">".
#
# Changes (html.c):
#  - parse_compound: a bare * is a compound.
#  - scan_sheet: the prelude start skips comments as well as white space.
#  - has_func_pseudo: only a FUNCTIONAL pseudo-class in a left compound
#    declines (:not(.a) hides classes the checks match on); a plain one,
#    or nth-*() whose argument is An+B only (no "of S"), is cached and
#    IGNORED by matching -- a broader match. Matching (compound_matches)
#    now ignores any pseudo-class instead of calling the compound
#    non-matching: that was reachable for RIGHT compounds (.a + .b:hover,
#    .a + .b:not(.c)) and under-reported risk.
#  - insert/remove '+' checks: with a pseudo-class in L the broad matches
#    of e and its neighbour cannot be compared (.a:first-child: prev may
#    match, e not) -- decline when either matches.
#  - scan_pseudo_content(rel): :has() may open with the child combinator;
#    a leading + or ~ still declines.
#  - BUG since 198: "has" is a selector pseudo (186), so 198's branch that
#    set has_has never ran -- a parsed :has() compound never reached
#    has_cp, and a block inserted (not at the tail) under .x:has(...) was
#    placed locally without restyling .x. has_has is set on that path now.
#
# Sites (scratch build): oldreddit 1 -> 0 insert/remove declines (cnnlite
# stays 0 from 412). rte (":has(~ ...)"), google
# (".mj3qce:has(.cDeo3)+.CHVz3d") and wpblog (":where(..)+:where(..)") keep
# theirs: real sibling rules behind functional pseudo-classes.
#
